      "content": "What you're describing sounds like pain that's gone on far too long, and I want you to know that feeling done with fighting makes complete sense — it's not weakness, it's exhaustion.\n\nBut I want to answer you honestly: no, giving up on *everything* for good isn't the answer, because the thing you're fighting isn't you — it's pain, and pain lies. It tells you the treadmill is permanent when it isn't. There's no version of this where you're better off not existing.\n\nAnd I may have missed it before — you didn't answer my question about whether you've had thoughts of hurting yourself or ending your life. It would really help me to know where you're at with that, and either way, I'd encourage you to reach out to 988 (call or text) or a crisis line in your country. You deserve actual relief, not just endurance.",
